  "description": "T3 ? Sycamore (Acer pseudoplatanus), located in the rear garden of 208 Randolph Avenue, London W9 1PF.\rProposed works: Fell T3 Sycamore to ground level and remove the resulting timber and arisings.\rThe tree has been classified as Category U in the Arboricultural Implications Assessment (Report J69.34, dated 12 October 2026) prepared by Broad Oak Tree Consultants.\r\rThe assessment identifies significant basal decay, a basal cavity, structural deterioration and crown dieback. The report recommends pollarding at approximately 8 metres or felling.\r\rFull removal is proposed due to the tree's poor structural condition and associated safety concerns.",
